From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KmsVsyncStop <kmsvs@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:30:00 
Subject: [PATCH 0118] gpu31-kms: bound decon_wait_for_vsync_thread so kthread_stop returns (int75)

The int74 load wedge is the vendor vsync thread:

    kthread_stop+0x70 <- decon_kms_put+0x1dc <- exynos7580_probe+0x154
    stuck: [s3c-fb-vsync] decon_wait_for_vsync_thread+0x58

decon_wait_for_vsync_thread() waits on `wait_event_interruptible` with a
condition that can never become true during teardown (pipe off) and never
checks kthread_should_stop(), so kthread_stop() blocks forever; the watchdog
does not fire because userspace is alive.

The loop now waits with a 100 ms timeout
(`wait_event_interruptible_timeout(..., HZ/10)`) and exits on
`kthread_should_stop() || decon->kms_teardown`.  decon_kms_teardown() already
sets the flag, turns the producer off (`decon_reg_set_int(..., 0)`) and wakes
`vsync_info.wait`/`wait_frmdone` before stopping, so the stop completes within
one poll interval.  The D-state skip remains only as a last resort.

--- a/drivers/video/exynos/decon_7580/decon-int_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/video/exynos/decon_7580/decon-int_drv.c
@@ -856,15 +856,24 @@
 {
 	struct decon_device *decon = data;
 
+	/*
+	 * int75: the vendor loop waits without a timeout, so kthread_stop()
+	 * blocked forever once the condition could no longer become true
+	 * (teardown with the pipe off).  Poll with a 100 ms timeout and exit
+	 * on kthread_should_stop()/kms_teardown, which bounds the stop.
+	 */
 	while (!kthread_should_stop()) {
 		ktime_t timestamp = decon->vsync_info.timestamp;
-		int ret = wait_event_interruptible(decon->vsync_info.wait,
+		int ret = wait_event_interruptible_timeout(decon->vsync_info.wait,
 			!ktime_equal(timestamp, decon->vsync_info.timestamp) &&
-			decon->vsync_info.active);
+			decon->vsync_info.active,
+			HZ / 10);
+
+		if (kthread_should_stop() || decon->kms_teardown)
+			break;
 
-		if (!ret) {
+		if (ret > 0)
 			sysfs_notify(&decon->dev->kobj, NULL, "vsync");
-		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
